   "body": "**Adversarial review (fable, cloud/review-1030-fable): APPROVE** — head fd2da4af\n\nThe three checks asked for:\n\n1. **Exact text: yes.** The diff is one line of `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` (item 10, line 297). The removed sentence and the added sentence are character for character the \"replace … by …\" of #955's `ledger-note`. Nothing else in the line changes.\n2. **Consistent with GAP-214 as #955's gap-edit sets it: yes.** #1029 (head 2b23ca56) folds the row to \"Same as legacy … the reader is pushed full width and hides the tab bar (#431)\", Gap `same`, H.1 `a`. The new sentence says the same thing.\n3. **Contradictions elsewhere: none introduced by the sentence itself.** GAP-008 (Plus readers keep the bar in Pro Max landscape), GAP-210, GAP-212, GAP-216, the UXD-24 line (404) and `docs/lots/LOT-082-adaptive-navigation.md:50` all agree with it.\n\nFindings (neither blocks):\n\n1. **Low — `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:322`.** \"The (b) rows include the ones the merged code already ships: … 212, 214\" stays as is. Once #1029 and this PR land, the row, the tally and item 10 all say 214 is `a`, while this prose still calls it a shipped (b) row. #1029 leaves that line untouched, and the fold script cannot edit prose. Fix: drop 214 from that list here or in a follow-up `ledger-notes` PR. The same line is already stale on dev-swift for 020, 022 (tally `a`) and 212 (row `a·master`).\n2. **Detail — merge order.** On dev-swift today row 240 still reads \"list and reader side by side … UX change … b\". If this PR merges before #1029, item 10 contradicts the row until #1029 lands. Fix: merge #1029 first, or both together.\n\n**Verified**\n- Worktree at fd2da4af: one commit on f53cb5df, one file, +1/−1; `git diff --check` clean.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/fold.py --check`: ok.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py guard` with the head ref `docs/ledger-notes-2026-11-17-955`: ok.\n- CI on the head: Docs consistency, Pre-commit, gitleaks and SwiftLint green; some Linux jobs were still running.\n- Read #955's body (merged as a764676e), #1029's GAP patch, and every mention of 212/214/216, #431, \"landscape\" and UXD-24 in the file.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
